11:02:33  INFO  [msg ← Uni] KP investigation closed with DIAGNOSIS + CANNOT (pending admin action). Relaying AS1's findings verbatim, plus my own confirmations:

=== AS1's diagnosis (verbatim) ===
1. `dig @4.2.2.1 acm.org` returns A 198.82.0.99 with the `aa` flag (TTL 0). The answer is hardcoded, not the result of a recursive lookup.
2. Process inspection on AS1: the listener on 4.2.2.1:53 is a dnsmasq launched with `--local=/acm.org/ --address=/acm.org/198.82.0.99`. It is the only process bound to 4.2.2.1:53 — there is no real recursive resolver behind it.
3. From AS1, 198.82.0.99 is unreachable (Host Unreachable from 198.82.0.254). 198.82.0.1 is reachable (94ms) and is the real ACM web server.
4. AS2's resolver (154.54.1.1) answers acm.org → 198.82.0.1, which matches the live host. So 198.82.0.99 is wrong, not a deliberate sinkhole.

ROOT CAUSE: AS1's recursive resolver is misconfigured — it serves a static, stale A record (198.82.0.99) for acm.org instead of recursing. Correct address is 198.82.0.1.

PROPOSED FIX (at AS1): remove the static override or change it to 198.82.0.1. Because this affects DNS service for all AS1 customers, AS1 will not apply it unilaterally — their admins have been notified. STATUS at AS1: CANNOT (pending admin action).

=== My (Uni) confirmations from 128.173.0.1 ===
- `dig acm.org @4.2.2.1` → 198.82.0.99 (still stale as of last check).
- `dig acm.org @154.54.1.1` (AS2) → 198.82.0.1 ✓
- ping 198.82.0.1 → 0% loss, 94ms ✓
- ping 198.82.0.99 → 100% loss, ICMP Host Unreachable from 198.82.0.254 ✓
- Your `curl --resolve acm.org:80:198.82.0.1` returning HTTP 200 confirms 198.82.0.1 is the live ACM web server.

=== Workaround options for you, immediately ===
(a) Add to /etc/hosts on your host: `198.82.0.1 acm.org www.acm.org`
(b) Or curl with --resolve as you already verified.
(I am NOT changing the campus DNS forwarder config unilaterally — that is an admin-controlled service that affects all campus users. If you'd like the campus resolver pointed away from 4.2.2.1, that requires admin approval here too.)

=== Uni KP status: CANNOT (pending AS1 admin action) ===
I will notify you immediately if AS1 reports the fix has been applied and I can re-verify acm.org resolves correctly end-to-end.
